eal part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form: \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then \(\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4}e^{-i\theta} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)\).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Substituting \(z\) and \(\frac{1}{z}\) into the expression, we get:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Simplifying the expression, we have:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m 4(75\cos\theta + 117i\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144i\cos\theta + 96i\sin\theta + 144\sin\theta).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Combining the real and imaginary parts, we get:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta) + i\left(4(117\cos\theta + 75\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(144\cos\theta + 96\sin\theta)\right).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m The real part of the expression is:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Simplifying further, we get:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta.[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m To find the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\), we can use the fact that the maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -432\), so the maximum value is:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540.[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(540\). The final answer is:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \boxed{540}[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [ground_truth] 540[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [score] 1.0[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [acc] True[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [pred] dapo:540,qwen:qwen_evaluated[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [dapo_result] {'score': 1.0, 'acc': True, 'pred': '540'}[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [qwen_result] {'score': 1.0, 'acc': True, 'pred': 'qwen_evaluated'}[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [dapo_correct] True[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [qwen_correct] True[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['reward']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['score']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['acc']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['pred']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['dapo_result']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['qwen_result']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['dapo_correct']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['qwen_correct']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m local_global_step_folder: ./checkpoints/STEER-F/pilot-steer-f-1p5b-s1-150/global_step_50[36m(WorkerDict pid=22767)[0m INFO:2026-09-30 16:43:17,368:[Rank 0] Saved model to /workspace/entropy_lora/checkpoints/STEER-F/pilot-steer-f-1p5b-s1-150/global_step_50/actor/model_world_size_4_rank_0.pt[36m(