lex number with \(|z| = 4\).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Therefore, \(\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4}e^{-i\theta} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)\).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Now, we substitute \(z = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\) and \(\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)\) into the expression:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Simplifying the expression, we get:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)),[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m and[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta) = \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta - 96i\sin\theta + 144i\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta) = \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Combining these, the expression becomes:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Separating the real and imaginary parts, we get:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \text{Real part} = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta),[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \text{Imaginary part} = 4(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta).[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m We are interested in the real part, so we focus on:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \text{Real part} = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta) = 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta.[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m To maximize \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\), we can use the fact that the maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -432\), so the maximum value is:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + (-432)^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540.[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(540\). The final answer is:[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \boxed{540}[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [ground_truth] 540[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [score] 1.0[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [acc] True[36m(TaskRunner pid=22143)[0m [pred] dapo:540,qwen:qwen_evaluated[36m(TaskRun